    "reasoning": "Nitpicks: Minor formatting (bullets vs another layout) is a nitpick; also the small preface text is fine.\n\nCritical issues:\n1) Missing required top-level transport mode: Screenshots 1 and 2 clearly show the top-level \"modes\" array contains four values: \"bus\", \"international-rail\", \"national-rail\", and \"tube\". The agent output omits \"international-rail\" and also presents the modes in a different order and with \"tube\" included but incomplete overall. This is a direct, evidenced mismatch on a required field.\n2) Latitude/longitude not supported by evidence: None of the provided screenshots show the lat/lon fields, so the agent\u2019s specific numeric coordinates (51.530782, -0.123802) are not grounded in the supplied visible official response excerpts. Given the task\u2019s strict \u201cuse the supplied official response\u201d constraint, reporting precise coordinates without visible support is effectively an unsupported claim relative to the evidence set.\n3) Zone value not supported/verified from the required location: The screenshots that show additionalProperties (e.g., screenshot 49) do not show any entry where key == \"Zone\". Therefore the agent\u2019s Zone=1 (and the claim it came from the key \"Zone\" entry) is not supported by the provided evidence.\n\nWhat the agent did get right: The StopPoint ID (HUBKGX) and commonName (King's Cross & St Pancras International) are explicitly visible in screenshot 49 and match. The Tube line identifiers list is also explicitly supported by screenshot 49 under lineModeGroups where modeName==\"tube\" (circle, hammersmith-city, metropolitan, northern, piccadilly, victoria), and the agent correctly excluded national-rail/bus identifiers.\n\nOutcome assessment: Because the task requires ALL of these fields to be reported correctly (ID, name, coordinates, every top-level mode, Zone, and Tube identifiers) and at least one required field is definitively wrong (missing \"international-rail\"), plus two other required fields (lat/lon and Zone-from-additionalProperties) are not substantiated by the provided evidence, an average user would not consider the task successfully completed as stated. The deliverable is an accurate extraction of a specific set of fields; that set is incomplete/incorrect.",
    "verifier_name": "mm_rubric_outcome",
    "metadata": {},
    "output_success": false,
    "primary_intent": "Extract specific fields from the official TfL StopPoint JSON response for HUBKGX: the StopPoint ID, common name, lat/lon, the complete top-level modes list, the Zone value specifically from additionalProperties where key==\"Zone\", and the Tube line identifiers specifically from the lineModeGroups entry where modeName==\"tube\". A reasonable user would not be flexible on missing/incorrect modes, wrong/made-up coordinates, or pulling Zone/Tube lines from the wrong part of the JSON, because the task is explicitly about accurate field extraction with strict source constraints."
  },
